{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== HANDOFF #11 — epic e369 + the new parity epic 3e73. READ THIS, THEN #10, THEN #9. ===\n\nWORKTREE /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-jira-family. ALWAYS: export PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\"\nDO NOT trust any board state below — it is a snapshot. Read the tickets.\n\n*** THE OPERATOR'S PRIORITY, STATED THIS SESSION AND IT REFRAMES THE WORK ***\n\"Our top priority is shipping defect-free Jira DC functionality. A related priority is ensuring\nthat our Jira DC testing contains parity with our existing Jira testing, because that will give us\nconfidence that we are shipping a defect-free feature.\"\nSo parity is INSTRUMENTAL, not adjacent. Epic 3e73's P1 children are DC-confidence work and are IN\nSCOPE alongside e369; its P2 children are Cloud-side hardening and must NOT gate DC. That framing\nis written into 3e73's description — read it before picking a child.\n\nBOARD AT WRITING: e369 26/30 closed (open: 727f, d103 at P1; 5200, cc77 at P2).\n3e73 0/6 (P1: cedc, 79d5, bd9e, 2944 — DC-confidence; P2: 0fad, 2127 — Cloud-side).\n\nMERGED THIS SESSION: 1177, 1179, 1182, 1183, 1185, 1186, 1188, 1190, 1191, 1202, 1203, 1206.\nCLOSED THIS SESSION: f2f3(S1), 9f0b, fe15, 6758(S2), b586, 6a91, 7f93, b9b8.\n\n--- WHAT EACH OPEN TICKET NEEDS ---\n * 727f (P1) — root cause PROVEN, fix written, NOT landed. It is BLOCKED on a real question, and an\n   agent is on it: the fix suppresses the differ's `field_drift` emission, and two orchestrate tests\n   about mutation COUNT then fail. Either the fix's premise (\"field sync is already owned by the\n   binding-aware phases\") is false and suppressing is DATA LOSS, or those tests drive a harness\n   where those phases never run and pin the MECHANISM. **Do not resolve it by relaxing the\n   assertions.** The recovered fix is local commit c207377b98 in the worktree\n   `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.claude/worktrees/agent-a1bf191c510431899`.\n * d103 (P1) — same subsystem as 727f, plausibly the same contract misuse; same agent owns both.\n   Reproduces with no Jira: `differ.compute_mutations({'KEY': entry}, {})` emits an outbound create.\n * 5200 (P2) — suite BUILT and landed, 43/49 green. Blocked on the bugs it found. See its latest\n   comment for the exact per-cell disposition; two of the six failures are already owned elsewhere\n   and one is a test-oracle fix this story owns.\n * cc77 (P2) — plan REWRITTEN and review-ready, last in the review agent's queue.\n   **NEVER run `rebar sign-review` on cc77**: its sidecar is from the OLD plan and would certify a\n   plan nobody reviewed. Its \"BLOCKING DISCOVERY\" comment is RETRACTED by two later comments.\n\n--- THE FIVE MISTAKES I MADE THIS SESSION. CARRY THESE; THEY ALL COST REAL TIME ---\n 1. **I DESTROYED AN AGENT'S UNCOMMITTED FIX** with `git checkout -- <file>` while undoing a\n    mutation check. `checkout --` restores from HEAD, and the fix had never been committed.\n    Recovered only by grepping the agent's JSONL transcript. **Copy the file aside, or commit,\n    before mutating. And tell every code-changing subagent to COMMIT EARLY AND OFTEN** — three\n    agents died mid-task this session (\"no progress for 600s\" / API error) and one lost work.\n 2. **AN UNCONTROLLED EXPERIMENT PRODUCED A CONFIDENT, WRONG, RECORDED CONCLUSION.** I \"proved\"\n    cc77's premise false by blaming a metaclass; my probe had varied TWO things (import path AND\n    local-vs-imported declaration). Controlled re-run: same class, shim import -> `Any`/no error,\n    real import -> `[attr-defined]`. The cause is that `rebar_reconciler` is a runtime `sys.path`\n    injection, not an importable package, so `ignore_missing_imports` widens it to `Any`. A\n    subagent caught me. **Vary one thing.**\n 3. **A MUTATION THAT GOES RED FOR THE WRONG REASON PROVES NOTHING.** My first 727f mutation\n    produced `reconcile_helpers.list(...)`; both cells failed on `AttributeError`, not on the\n    suppression's absence. Check the failure MESSAGE matches the property you meant to break.\n 4. **I REMOVED THE ALL-SKIP CANARY FROM THE TWO MODULES THAT MATTER MOST** by refactoring\n    `_live_jira_ready` out of them (change 1182). `tests/external/conftest.py` marks `jira_live`\n    only on modules defining that name. Measured: collected=0 before, 29 after. Fixed in 1203.\n 5. **I over-read a green.** I recorded \"J11 IS COMPLETE\" on a 26/26 harness run; five ACs were\n    unmet. A green harness is not a green story.\n\n--- GERRIT / GATE MECHANICS LEARNED THIS SESSION ---\n * An `LLM-Review -1` tagged `coverage-gap (…)` is an INFRA VETO, not your code\n   (docs/review-policy.md has the table). For `llm-unavailable` the doc says re-push — but Gerrit\n   rejects an identical push (\"no new changes\"), and `--amend --no-edit` produces a patchset with\n   the SAME TREE, so Gerrit COPIES the stale vote forward and the bot does not re-review.\n   **The fix is `DELETE /a/changes/<n>/reviewers/<bot>/votes/LLM-Review` as an admin** — a label-0\n   POST from another account does NOT clear someone else's vote. Operator authorised\n   `JoeOakhartNava` for re-triggering only.\n * `rebar transition <id> ... --ref <sha>` verifies the close against a COMMITTED TREE instead of\n   HEAD. Use it when agents share the worktree, or to close against a stacked commit. It is cleaner\n   than moving HEAD and hoping.\n * A PARENT's close can fail `stale-pin-drift` because a CHILD's plan changed after the parent was\n   reviewed. Re-run `rebar review-plan <parent>` and retry.\n * `rebar` is an EDITABLE install from this checkout, so parking the worktree on an old commit\n   DOWNGRADES the tool. A review crashed with `CriteriaError: unknown prompt 'plan-review-G7'`\n   purely because HEAD predated that prompt file.\n * NEVER use `FETCH_HEAD` while a background job is fetching — it is one file per repo and a\n   concurrent fetch clobbers it. Check out an explicit sha. This put me on an unrelated commit and\n   made a close gate report that `_backend.py` \"does not exist\"."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785687926666495001,"uuid":"7eb3fd1d-550e-40f4-a6a1-3a65bde07ffd"}